From 4930a515498e1b5977740a8302205cb3ff6bf75b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3351/3799] soh: rename func_800E64F8 ->
 AudioThread_ClearChannelIo

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: queues the same command with every field zero
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_thread.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_thread.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c b/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
index 42aa22198..7d72034a1 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
@@ -776,7 +776,8 @@ void AudioThread_SetChannelIo(s32 arg0, s32 arg1, s32 arg2) {
     Audio_QueueCmdS32(((arg0 & 0xFF) << 0x10) | 0xFA000000 | ((arg1 & 0xFF) << 8) | (arg2 & 0xFF), 1);
 }
 
-void func_800E64F8(void) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800E64F8: queues the same command with every field zero
+void AudioThread_ClearChannelIo(void) {
     Audio_QueueCmdS32(0xFA000000, 0);
 }
 
